      "https://engineering.stanford.edu/news/stanfords-code-place-introductory-programming-course-offers-new-model-large-scale-interactive"
    ],
    "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
    "notes": "Edition: the current official public syllabus (codeinplace.stanford.edu, used for the 2024/2025 runs; 2026 run starts Apr 2026) gives 6 weeks: W1 Control Flow with Karel (build: Welcome Karel), W2 The Art of Coding (Puzzle Karel), W3 Console Programs (Sandcastles), W4 Understanding Variables (Khansole Academy), W5 Graphics (Random Art), W6 Lists + Dictionaries (World's Hardest Game), then 'Beyond': Final Project. The in-app week labels differ slightly (W4 'Python Control Flow', W6 'Lists + Dicts'), and 2024 section-leader materials label W4 'Python Control Flow'. Week-level topics and the 'You Build' assignments are verified from the official site. Individual LESSON titles live behind login (Firestore) and could not be fetched; the per-lesson modules here are a reconstruction that splits each week into its lessons using the CS106A lecture titles CIP has historically reused (Intro to Karel, Control Flow, Decomposition, Intro to Python/Variables, Expressions, Control Flow Revisited, Functions Revisited/parameters, Graphics, Animation, Lists, Dictionaries) plus the 'Random' lesson referenced in the site's Khansole Academy materials. Exact lesson names/boundaries may differ; the 'Animation' lesson in W5 and the placement of parameters/return (W4 vs W5; a 2024 section placed it in W5 with graphics) are the least certain. Section problems listed in projects (e.g. Hospital Karel, Planetary Weight, High-Low, Heads Up) come from one 2024 section leader's repo and are marked '(section)'. Earlier editions differed: 2020/2021 were ~5 weeks + final project and included Images (SimpleImage), Text Processing, Files and Data Science; Images is NOT in the 2023+ syllabus, so no images module is included. No certificate grade; completion requires assignments in all three units (Karel, Console, Graphics) and attending sections."
  },
